-- title:
--   Localised Hecke algebra as a cohomological corner ring
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a set $S$ of naturals containing no prime divisor of $N$, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$; assume the weight-two forms of level $N$ have an integral structure, i.e. [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spans $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ over $\mathbb{C}$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$). On the side of $H^1$: the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily N ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen N S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) (symbols $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and diamonds $\langle d\rangle$, realised as transfer operators `heckeTL` and `diamondL` on [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162)) are assumed to commute pairwise, and $\bar\theta$ assigns to each generator a value in $k$ agreeing with $\theta(T_\ell)$ and $\theta(U_q)$ on the $T$- and $U$-generators (no condition is imposed on the diamond generators). Let $B$ be the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by the range of these operators, let $Sp$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $B$ (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $B$ and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j\iff i\neq j$), let $i_0$ be an index, and let $\pi_k$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map from the corner ring $e_{i_0}Be_{i_0}$ to $k$ carrying the corner image of each generator's operator to $\bar\theta$ of that generator. Assume the non-Eisenstein condition: some prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ satisfies $\ell\equiv 1 \pmod N$ and $\theta(T_\ell)\neq \ell+1$ in $k$. Then there is an isomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras between [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisation of the Hecke algebra data at the multiplicative submonoid `heckeLocalSubmonoid N S 𝒪 θ` attached to $\theta$) and the corner ring $e_{i_0}Be_{i_0}$, carrying the image under the structure map [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) of each $T_\ell$, respectively each $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, to the corner image of the corresponding cohomological operator.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura comparison at a non-Eisenstein maximal ideal: the localised weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$ is identified, compatibly with all $T_\ell$ and $U_q$, with a corner ring of the Hecke algebra acting on $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal{O})$. It feeds the cohomological arguments at auxiliary level and the Ihara-type and level-lowering steps that invoke it, notably [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_residueChar_gammaZero`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_residueChar_gammaZero).
